        <button id="options" onclick="document.getElementById('whatToDo').style.display = 'block'">What was this feature meant to do?</button>
        <div id="whatToDo" style="display: none">
          <p> This feature will allow you to post an Arena such as a birthday party or a bash so that other comrades can join you event</p>
          <p>This feature will also allow you to subscribe to an announcer e.g. your classrep and view announcements from them, or rather become an announcer so people can subscribe to your announcements.</p>
          <p>We decided to disable this feature for now to avoid overwhelming our users with too many features at once, and to focus on perfecting the core experience of MMUN.</p>
          <div>
            <button onclick="document.getElementById('whatToDo').style.display = 'none'">Got it!</button>
            <button class="voteBtn" id="voteToComeTrue" onclick=" 
              document.querySelectorAll('.voteBtn').forEach(btn => btn.style.display='none');alert('Thankyou for the vote.'); 
              sendfeedback('true','notics');
            ">Bring this feature</button>
           <button class="voteBtn" id="voteToComeFalse" 
            onclick="
              document.querySelectorAll('.voteBtn').forEach(btn => btn.style.display='none');
              alert('Thanks for voting'); 
              sendfeedback('false','notics'); 
            ">
            Don't bring this feature
      </button>
            <button class="voteBtn" id="voteToComeNeutral" 
            onclick="
              document.querySelectorAll('.voteBtn').forEach(btn => btn.style.display='none');
              alert('Thanks for the opinion'); x
              sendfeedback('improve', 'jobs'); 
            ">
            Improve current features</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
